{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790564800288,"sessionID":"ses_f1a065858ffecI4EzBIBVNcH78","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_7pTemk0lJwunyl7aCWy9lrim","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Final Closeout Summary\n2: \n3: The controlling reimbursement cap is **$1,600.00**, set by the 2026-05-22 award update (`03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`), which supersedes the original $2,000.00 cap in the 2026-04-15 award letter (`02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`).\n4: \n5: The corrected reimbursable total is **$1,588.00**, leaving **$12.00** under the cap.\n6: \n7: Useful prior work preserved: the supported decisions to approve garden supplies (G-001) and accessibility printing (G-003), reject staff gifts (G-004), and the recorded outcomes of 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed for accessible pickup locations.\n8: \n9: Prior work corrected: G-002 refreshments are capped at $120.00 rather than the requested $145.00; G-005 is rejected because its $310.00 expense has no receipt despite the over-$75.00 receipt requirement and general public outreach printing is not listed as eligible; and the draft's use of the superseded $2,000.00 cap and its $145.00 remaining calculation are replaced. The omitted G-006 final report postage expense ($68.00) is approved under the eligible postage rule and ledger-note exception to the receipt requirement.\n10: \n11: Program outcomes (`05_outcomes.md`): **140** seedling starter kits were distributed; **36** Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations; and **18** volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n\n(End of file - total 11 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe controlling reimbursement cap is **$1,600.00**, set by the 2026-05-22 award update (`03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`), which supersedes the original $2,000.00 cap in the 2026-04-15 award letter (`02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`).\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is **$1,588.00**, leaving **$12.00** under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work preserved: the supported decisions to approve garden supplies (G-001) and accessibility printing (G-003), reject staff gifts (G-004), and the recorded outcomes of 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed for accessible pickup locations.\n\nPrior work corrected: G-002 refreshments are capped at $120.00 rather than the requested $145.00; G-005 is rejected because its $310.00 expense has no receipt despite the over-$75.00 receipt requirement and general public outreach printing is not listed as eligible; and the draft's use of the superseded $2,000.00 cap and its $145.00 remaining calculation are replaced. The omitted G-006 final report postage expense ($68.00) is approved under the eligible postage rule and ledger-note exception to the receipt requirement.\n\nProgram outcomes (`05_outcomes.md`): **140** seedling starter kits were distributed; **36** Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations; and **18** volunteer setup shifts were completed.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","text":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe controlling reimbursement cap is **$1,600.00**, set by the 2026-05-22 award update (`03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`), which supersedes the original $2,000.00 cap in the 2026-04-15 award letter (`02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`).\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is **$1,588.00**, leaving **$12.00** under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work preserved: the supported decisions to approve garden supplies (G-001) and accessibility printing (G-003), reject staff gifts (G-004), and the recorded outcomes of 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed for accessible pickup locations.\n\nPrior work corrected: G-002 refreshments are capped at $120.00 rather than the requested $145.00; G-005 is rejected because its $310.00 expense has no receipt despite the over-$75.00 receipt requirement and general public outreach printing is not listed as eligible; and the draft's use of the superseded $2,000.00 cap and its $145.00 remaining calculation are replaced. The omitted G-006 final report postage expense ($68.00) is approved under the eligible postage rule and ledger-note exception to the receipt requirement.\n\nProgram outcomes (`05_outcomes.md`): **140** seedling starter kits were distributed; **36** Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations; and **18** volunteer setup shifts were completed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":11,"totalLines":11,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","time":{"start":1790564800254,"end":1790564800287}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0dd55da6b44e073d016ab9d9c00d4887d291d0204de61ac12d"}},"id":"prt_0e5fa96f2001QwqlKi01yqZkhE","sessionID":"ses_f1a065858ffecI4EzBIBVNcH78","messageID":"msg_0e5fa84e6001PVjTUj2hEFMPjq"}}
